:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDMSGD.Add Message Description (ADDMSGD)
:P.Use the Add Message Description (ADDMSGD) command to add a message
description to a message file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/MSG'.First-level message text (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/SECLVL'.Second-level message text (SECLVL)
:P.The second-level text of the message&colon. what it means and what to
do.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/SEV'.Severity code (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/FMT'.Message data fields (FMT)
:P.The message data fields for this command.
:P.Up to 99 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Data type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *QUAL, *CCHAR, *BIN, *QTDCHAR, *UBIN, *ITV,
*DTS, *UTC, *UTCD, *UTCT, *SYSPTR, *SPP.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VARY.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Decimal positions
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/TYPE'.Reply type (TYPE)
:P.The reply type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:PT.:PK.*NAME:EPK.
:PD.By name.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALPHA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/LEN'.Reply length (LEN)
:P.The reply length for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Decimal positions
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/VALUES'.Valid reply values (VALUES)
:P.The replies that are valid for the message.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/SPCVAL'.Special reply values (SPCVAL)
:P.The special reply values for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. From value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. To value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/RANGE'.Range of reply values (RANGE)
:P.The range of reply values for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Lower value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Upper value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/REL'.Relationship for reply (REL)
:P.The relationship for reply for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relational operator
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EQ:EPK.
:PD.Equal to.
:PT.:PK.*LE:EPK.
:PD.Less than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GE:EPK.
:PD.Greater than or equal to.
:PT.:PK.*GT:EPK.
:PD.Greater than.
:PT.:PK.*LT:EPK.
:PD.Less than.
:PT.:PK.*NE:EPK.
:PD.Not equal to.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:PT.:PK.*NG:EPK.
:PD.Not greater than.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/DFT'.Default reply value (DFT)
:P.The default reply, used when the message is not answered.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/DFTPGM'.Default program (DFTPGM)
:P.The default program for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/DMPLST'.Data to be dumped (DMPLST)
:P.The data to be dumped for this command.
:P.Up to 102 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *JOBINT, *JOBDMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/ALROPT'.Alert options (ALROPT)
:P.Whether an alert is sent when the message is sent, and when.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Alert option
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UNATTEND.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Resource name variable
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/LOGPRB'.Log problem (LOGPRB)
:P.Whether a problem is logged for the message.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDMSGD/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDRPYLE.Add Reply List Entry (ADDRPYLE)
:P.Use the Add Reply List Entry (ADDRPYLE) command to add an entry to
the system reply list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRPYLE/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRPYLE/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRPYLE/CMPDTA'.Comparison data (CMPDTA)
:P.The comparison data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Comparison data
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 28 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRPYLE/RPY'.Message reply (RPY)
:P.The message reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDRPYLE/DMPJOB'.Dump job (DMPJOB)
:P.Whether to dump job.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGMSGD.Change Message Description (CHGMSGD)
