:HELP NAME='CHGMSGD/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGMSGF.Change Message File (CHGMSGF)
:P.Use the Change Message File (CHGMSGF) command to change a message
file's text and CCSID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGF/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MSGD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGMSGQ.Change Message Queue (CHGMSGQ)
:P.Use the Change Message Queue (CHGMSGQ) command to change a message
queue's delivery mode and attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/DLVRY'.Delivery (DLVRY)
:P.How messages arriving on the queue are delivered&colon. interrupting
the user, notifying, holding, or calling a program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*HOLD:EPK.
:PD.Held.
:PT.:PK.*NOTIFY:EPK.
:PD.The user is notified that a message arrived.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BREAK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/PGM'.Break handling program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DSPMSG.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/SEV'.Severity code filter (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/RESET'.Reset old messages (RESET)
:P.Whether to reset old messages.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/ALWALT'.Allow alerts (ALWALT)
:P.The allow alerts for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGMSGQ/MSGQFULL'.Queue full action (MSGQFULL)
:P.The queue full action for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SNDRCV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGRPYLE.Change Reply List Entry (CHGRPYLE)
:P.Use the Change Reply List Entry (CHGRPYLE) command to change an entry
of the system reply list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRPYLE/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRPYLE/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRPYLE/CMPDTA'.Comparison data (CMPDTA)
:P.The comparison data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Comparison data
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 28 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRPYLE/RPY'.Message reply (RPY)
:P.The message reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGRPYLE/DMPJOB'.Dump job (DMPJOB)
:P.The dump job for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLRMSGQ.Clear Message Queue (CLRMSGQ)
:P.Use the Clear Message Queue (CLRMSGQ) command to remove the messages
on a message queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRMSGQ/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRMSGQ/CLEAR'.Messages to clear (CLEAR)
:P.The messages to clear for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEEPUNANS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTMSGF.Create Message File (CRTMSGF)
:P.Use the Create Message File (CRTMSGF) command to create a message
file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGF/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGF/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGF/SIZE'.Message file size (SIZE)
:P.The message file size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial storage size (KB)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 16384.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment (KB)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 16384.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 2 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGF/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MSGD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGF/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTMSGQ.Create Message Queue (CRTMSGQ)
:P.Use the Create Message Queue (CRTMSGQ) command to create a message
queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/FORCE'.Force to auxiliary storage (FORCE)
:P.Whether to force to auxiliary storage.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/SIZE'.Message queue size (SIZE)
:P.The message queue size for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Initial storage size (KB)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16384.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 5 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Increment (KB)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16384.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Maximum increments
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/ALWALT'.Allow alerts (ALWALT)
:P.Whether to allow alerts.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/MSGQFULL'.Queue full action (MSGQFULL)
:P.The queue full action for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, no more messages are added.
:PT.:PK.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SNDRCV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTMSGQ/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTMSGF.Delete Message File (DLTMSGF)
:P.Use the Delete Message File (DLTMSGF) command to delete one or more
message files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTMSGF/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTMSGQ.Delete Message Queue (DLTMSGQ)
:P.Use the Delete Message Queue (DLTMSGQ) command to delete one or more
message queues.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTMSGQ/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPLOG.Display Log (DSPLOG)
:P.Use the Display Log (DSPLOG) command to show the history log over a
period, by job or message.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLOG/LOG'.Log (LOG)
:P.The log for this command.
:P.The value must be QHST.
:P.When no value is given, QHST is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLOG/PERIOD'.Time period (PERIOD)
:P.The time period for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BEGIN.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLOG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*PRTWRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the messages are printed and the queue starts over.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRTSECLVL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLOG/JOB'.Jobs (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLOG/MSGID'.Message identifiers (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.Up to 100 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPMSG.Display Messages (DSPMSG)
:P.Use the Display Messages (DSPMSG) command to show the messages on a
message queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WRKUSR, *ALLWS.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*COPY:EPK.
:PD.A copy.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/START'.Start position (START)
:P.The start position for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/SEV'.Severity code filter (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSG/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPMSGD.Display Message Description (DSPMSGD)
:P.Use the Display Message Description (DSPMSGD) command to show message
descriptions from a message file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSGD/RANGE'.Range of message identifiers (RANGE)
:P.The range of message identifiers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Lower value
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Upper value
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSGD/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSGD/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSGD/FMTTXT'.Format message text (FMTTXT)
:P.Whether to format message text.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPMSGD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MRGMSGF.Merge Message File (MRGMSGF)
:P.Use the Merge Message File (MRGMSGF) command to copy message
descriptions from one message file into another, keeping the replaced
ones in a third if asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGMSGF/FROMMSGF'.From message file (FROMMSGF)
:P.The from message file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGMSGF/TOMSGF'.To message file (TOMSGF)
:P.The to message file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGMSGF/RPLMSGF'.Replaced message file (RPLMSGF)
:P.The replaced message file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGMSGF/SELECT'.Message identifiers (SELECT)
:P.The message identifiers for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OVRMSGF.Override with Message File (OVRMSGF)
:P.Use the Override with Message File (OVRMSGF) command to have another
message file looked at first.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRMSGF/MSGF'.Message file being overridden (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRMSGF/TOMSGF'.Overriding to message file (TOMSGF)
:P.The overriding to message file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRMSGF/SECURE'.Secure from other overrides (SECURE)
:P.Whether the file is protected from overrides at earlier call levels.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OVRMSGF/OVRSCOPE'.Override scope (OVRSCOPE)
:P.The scope of the override&colon. the call level, the activation group
or the job.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTGRPDFN:EPK.
:PD.As the activation group defines it.
:PT.:PK.*CALLLVL:EPK.
:PD.The call level.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCVMSG.Receive Message (RCVMSG)
:P.Use the Receive Message (RCVMSG) command to receive a message into CL
variables, from a call stack entry's queue or a named message queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/PGMQ'.Call stack entry message queue (PGMQ)
:P.The call stack entry message queue for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relationship
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Call stack entry
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *, *CTLBDY, *PGMBDY, *PGMNAME.
:P.Module&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Bound program&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PGMQ.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*NEXT:EPK.
:PD.The next one.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*NOTIFY:EPK.
:PD.The user is notified that a message arrived.
:PT.:PK.*COPY:EPK.
:PD.A copy.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RPY, *COMP, *DIAG, *EXCP, *RQS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGKEY'.Message key (MSGKEY)
:P.The message key for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TOP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/WAIT'.Wait time (seconds) (WAIT)
:P.The wait time (seconds) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits. The value must be from 0 to
9999999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/RMV'.Remove message (RMV)
:P.The remove message for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *KEEPEXCP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/KEYVAR'.CL var for KEYVAR (4) (KEYVAR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of KEYVAR. Give a character
variable of at least 4 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSG'.CL var for MSG (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGLEN'.CL var for MSGLEN (5 0) (MSGLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of MSGLEN. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/SECLVL'.CL var for SECLVL (SECLVL)
:P.The second-level text of the message&colon. what it means and what to
do.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/SECLVLLEN'.CL var for SECLVLLEN (5 0) (SECLVLLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SECLVLLEN. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGDTA'.CL var for MSGDTA (MSGDTA)
:P.The values substituted for the message's variables.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGDTALEN'.CL var for MSGDTALEN (5 0) (MSGDTALEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of MSGDTALEN. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGID'.CL var for MSGID (7) (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/SEV'.CL var for SEV (2 0) (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/SENDER'.CL var for SENDER (SENDER)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SENDER. Give a character
variable of at least 720 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 720 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/RTNTYPE'.CL var for RTNTYPE (2) (RTNTYPE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of RTNTYPE. Give a character
variable of at least 2 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/ALROPT'.CL var for ALROPT (9) (ALROPT)
:P.Whether an alert is sent when the message is sent, and when.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 9 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGF'.CL var for MSGF (10) (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/MSGFLIB'.CL var for MSGFLIB (10) (MSGFLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of MSGFLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/TXTCCSID'.CL var for TXTCCSID (5 0) (TXTCCSID)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of TXTCCSID. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVMSG/DTACCSID'.CL var for DTACCSID (5 0) (DTACCSID)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of DTACCSID. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVMSG.Remove Message (RMVMSG)
:P.Use the Remove Message (RMVMSG) command to remove one message or a
group of them from a queue.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSG/PGMQ'.Call stack entry message queue (PGMQ)
:P.The call stack entry message queue for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relationship
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Call stack entry
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *, *CTLBDY, *PGMBDY, *PGMNAME.
:P.Module&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Bound program&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSG/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PGMQ.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSG/MSGKEY'.Message key (MSGKEY)
:P.The message key for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSG/CLEAR'.Messages to remove (CLEAR)
:P.The messages to remove for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BYKEY, *KEEPUNANS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVMSGD.Remove Message Description (RMVMSGD)
:P.Use the Remove Message Description (RMVMSGD) command to remove a
message description from a message file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSGD/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVMSGD/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVRPYLE.Remove Reply List Entry (RMVRPYLE)
:P.Use the Remove Reply List Entry (RMVRPYLE) command to remove one
entry, or all of them, from the reply list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVRPYLE/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 4 digits. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDBRKMSG.Send Break Message (SNDBRKMSG)
:P.Use the Send Break Message (SNDBRKMSG) command to send an immediate
message that breaks in at work station message queues.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDBRKMSG/MSG'.Message text (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 512 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDBRKMSG/TOMSGQ'.To work station message queue (TOMSGQ)
:P.The message queue the message is sent to.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLWS.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDBRKMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDBRKMSG/RPYMSGQ'.Message queue to get reply (RPYMSGQ)
:P.The message queue to get reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYSOPR is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDMSG.Send Message (SNDMSG)
:P.Use the Send Message (SNDMSG) command to send an immediate message to
users or message queues.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDMSG/MSG'.Message text (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 512 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDMSG/TOUSR'.To user profile (TOUSR)
:P.The to user profile for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLACT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDMSG/TOMSGQ'.To message queue (TOMSGQ)
:P.The message queue the message is sent to.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDMSG/RPYMSGQ'.Message queue to get reply (RPYMSGQ)
:P.The message queue to get reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDPGMMSG.Send Program Message (SNDPGMMSG)
:P.Use the Send Program Message (SNDPGMMSG) command to send a message
from a CL program to a call stack entry, a message queue or a user.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/MSGDTA'.Message data field values (MSGDTA)
:P.The values substituted for the message's variables.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/MSG'.Message text (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/TOPGMQ'.To call stack entry queue (TOPGMQ)
:P.The to call stack entry queue for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Relationship
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Call stack entry
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *, *CTLBDY, *PGMBDY, *PGMNAME.
:P.Module&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Bound program&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/TOMSGQ'.To message queue (TOMSGQ)
:P.The message queue the message is sent to.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TOPGMQ.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/TOUSR'.To user profile (TOUSR)
:P.The to user profile for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLACT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*NOTIFY:EPK.
:PD.The user is notified that a message arrived.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COMP, *DIAG, *ESCAPE, *RQS, *STATUS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/RPYMSGQ'.Message queue to get reply (RPYMSGQ)
:P.The message queue to get reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PGMQ.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/KEYVAR'.CL var for KEYVAR (4) (KEYVAR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of KEYVAR. Give a character
variable of at least 4 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPGMMSG/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDRPYMSG.Send Reply Message (SNDRPYMSG)
:P.Use the Send Reply Message (SNDRPYMSG) command to answer an inquiry
message by its key.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRPYMSG/MSGKEY'.Message key (MSGKEY)
:P.The message key for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRPYMSG/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRPYMSG/RPY'.Reply (RPY)
:P.The reply for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRPYMSG/RMV'.Remove message (RMV)
:P.Whether to remove message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRPYMSG/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDUSRMSG.Send User Message (SNDUSRMSG)
:P.Use the Send User Message (SNDUSRMSG) command to send a message from
a CL program and, for an inquiry, wait for the reply.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSGDTA'.Message data field values (MSGDTA)
:P.The values substituted for the message's variables.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSG'.Message text (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 512 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/VALUES'.Valid replies (VALUES)
:P.The replies that are valid for the message.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/DFT'.Default reply (DFT)
:P.The default reply, used when the message is not answered.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/TOMSGQ'.To message queue (TOMSGQ)
:P.The message queue the message is sent to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*EXT:EPK.
:PD.Extended.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/TOUSR'.To user profile (TOUSR)
:P.The to user profile for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:PT.:PK.*REQUESTER:EPK.
:PD.The user or device of the job that runs the command.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/MSGRPY'.CL var for MSGRPY (MSGRPY)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of MSGRPY. Give a character
variable of at least 132 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDUSRMSG/TRNTBL'.Translate table (TRNTBL)
:P.The translate table for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMSG.Work with Messages (WRKMSG)
:P.Use the Work with Messages (WRKMSG) command to show the messages of a
message queue, answer them and remove them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the workstation.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The message queue of the user profile.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.QSYSOPR, the system operator's message queue.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WRKUSR, *ALLWS.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/MSGTYPE'.Message type (MSGTYPE)
:P.The type of the message&colon. informational, inquiry, completion,
diagnostic, escape and so on.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*INFO:EPK.
:PD.An informational message.
:PT.:PK.*INQ:EPK.
:PD.An inquiry message, which waits for a reply.
:PT.:PK.*COPY:EPK.
:PD.A copy.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/START'.Start position (START)
:P.The start position for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/SEV'.Severity code filter (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSG/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMSGD.Work with Message Descriptions (WRKMSGD)
:P.Use the Work with Message Descriptions (WRKMSGD) command to show the
message descriptions of a message file and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSGD/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSGD/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QCPFMSG is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMSGQ.Work with Message Queues (WRKMSGQ)
:P.Use the Work with Message Queues (WRKMSGQ) command to show a list of
message queues and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMSGQ/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKRPYLE.Work with Reply List Entries (WRKRPYLE)
:P.Use the Work with Reply List Entries (WRKRPYLE) command to show the
entries of the system reply list and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRPYLE/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
